  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "0.4 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 34,021 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Wikipedia vocabulary added",
   "text": "28,202 of the reference words come from a Wikipedia corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, snd_wikipedia_2021_100K, 1.9 million words); 5,819 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words. Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abjad: CV is orthographic",
   "text": "Sindhi is written without short vowels. CV here is orthographic: alif, waw and ye count as V; the aspiration marker (ھ) is a modifier. Diacritics were removed."
  }
 ],
